Description:
    Eject a crosswire component out of the gem and into your own app, so you own and
    can freely edit the copy. See docs/DECISIONS.md D6 for the full rationale.

    Tiers:

      --markup (default)   Copies the component's partial to
                            app/views/crosswire/_<name>.html.erb. You still receive
                            a11y wiring, controller fixes and presenter changes from
                            the gem — only the markup shape is now yours.

      --controller          Copies the partial (if the component has one) AND its
                            Stimulus controller to
                            app/javascript/controllers/<name>_controller.js, meant to
                            be re-registered under your own identifier. Full
                            ownership — you stop receiving fixes for the controller.

      --all                 Copies every component's markup (markup tier only).

    Not every component owns a partial. Behaviours that decorate existing elements
    (dismiss, persist, transition, autosubmit, intersection, clipboard, focus-trap)
    ship no markup of their own — only widgets like disclosure, dialog and confirm
    do. Ejecting a partial-less component without --controller prints an explanation
    instead of writing anything.

    Never overwrites an existing ejected file without --force.

Example:
    rails generate crosswire:eject disclosure

        Ejects app/views/crosswire/_disclosure.html.erb.

    rails generate crosswire:eject disclosure --controller

        Ejects the partial AND app/javascript/controllers/disclosure_controller.js.
        Full ownership of both.

    rails generate crosswire:eject --all

        Ejects every component's partial.

    rails generate crosswire:eject disclosure --force

        Re-ejects, overwriting your existing copy.
